--- An interpolation's text is read on its own, and what its reading
--- refuses is placed at the line of the string holding it: a bracket that
--- closes nothing inside a string on line 9 had been shown on line 1, a
--- line that holds no interpolation (Rosetta Code, Unicode strings)

x = 1
log[x]
log['`x + 1`']
log['`x + )`']
